 squads and duo's as to post a solo in  my opinion using this weapon leaves you  open to base rushers and you can be  killed while using it and no one is  watching your back in solo it's also  very nice for long distance fights or  when the opponent is distracted if two  people are fighting go for one of them  since they'll be more occupied on the  person in front of them and then not you  about 20 miles away with the missile  launcher you can also use the missile  launcher if you want to to get a  bird's-eye view let's say you're  chilling up on the top of a hill and you  can't see below you basically just look  up in the air and you're gonna get a  bird's-eye view of the people around you  and all their bases in the clip we were  fighting a team atop a hill and when I  went to missile launched the team at the  bottom I spotted another team that was  rushing us which if I didn't discover  them could have gotten us killed so this  weapon is very good for surveillance now  now not only is it good for kill  it's also good for rocket riding rocket  riding using an RPG used to get you  killed a lot since if you left your very  left open in the middle of nowhere  especially if the enemies are directly  ahead of you  now you can swerve and maneuver all you  want to a base it's like another form of  base rushing but a lot slower if you  transport your team and yourself if you  detach the rocket before it hits and  base rush an opposing squad on top of  the transporting the team you can also  blow up their base simultaneously while  transporting your team since obviously a  rocket launcher so basically you're  multitasking with the weapon if you're  in a teamfight like in the clip I had my  buddies distract the people in front of  us while I blasted them to bits from the  back this is so much fun and I can't  stress it enough how fun this weapon was  to use the first time we got it for one  not to use the weapon though it  definitely has to be close range or solo  play especially if you're at the end of  the game well you can use the launcher  in the endgame and that's completely  fine keep in mind that you may not be  the only one with the missile launcher  and since you're controlling it it can  leave you exposed you can get flanked  and not even know about it  it still works if you want to get a  bird's-eye view of opposing enemies but  just be careful since you're obviously  vulnerable to attacks and if it's the  end game there's not going to be lots of  noise since people are going to be  hiding in their bases and then they're  going to see the RPG and know exactly  where their next targets going to be  it's definitely more beneficial to use a  rocket launcher in a close-range fight  since it's faster than the missile  launcher and you know have to be locked  in the animation for it so if you happen  to be close range or in a building use  the regular rocket launcher instead as  opposed to the missile launcher I'm not  saying that if you're in solos don't  ever use the missile launcher you can  use it as just as much as you want you  just have to be a lot more cautious of  your surroundings when you do so one  other quick thing that I noticed is  during when I was playing with the  missile launcher is that it's also very  nice to pair with if you have a sniper  rifle the semi-automatic or the bolt it  doesn't really matter all you need to  know about is the scope since obviously  the sniper has the longest scope and you  can see very far you can spot people  from a mile away and then use your  missile launcher to go actually do the  damage and if you don't want to use the  sniper I found out that that was pretty  useful since obviously like I said the  sniper has lots of range so you could  basically see the whole map roughly or  that area that you're in depending on  how big the circle is you can see  everybody around you and spot out  everyone for my overall thoughts though  this weapon does a lot of damage which  is obvious since it is a rocket launcher  but my only problem is that it can be a  little bit overpowered especially when  you're on the receiving end in someone  rushing you while the other guy hangs  and shoots missiles from afar so that is  a bit overpowered but it does have its  drawbacks that being that you have to be  stationary when controlling it which  could cause people to flank you or rush  you without you knowing and the fact  that there's a smoke trail that travels  behind it so you know where the initial  rocket was fired making easier for you  to find that person shooting it for  comparing in terms of other weapons  similar to it comparing the to the  grenade launcher this is a way better  choice it could shoot farther and you  can obviously guide the rocket or you  want to go as opposed to the grenade  launcher where it it goes far but not as  far as the missile launcher and it just  does a lot more damage compared to the  regular rocket launcher it depends on  the situation if you're in a close  engagement with the team or an enemy use  a rocket launcher if you're in squads or  duo's and have the team rush up and  distract them while you flank around  with the missile launcher that's fine  too or you can sit in a comfy base with  your buddies get a cozy campfire down  and get a bird's-eye view of the people  or pick off people from the comfort of  your own base either situation is fine  as well but that is going to be the end  of the video like I said just the cue a  few quick tips to definitely nail into  it's very good in squads especially if  you want to be that dude that hangs back  sits in your own mini base and just  shoots from afar while they're getting  distracted because obviously they have  to focus on the rocket launcher and the  teammates rushing though it's definitely  very useful in a squads and duos  environment and then just be wary if you  are using it the people around you just  in case you happen to get rushed up on  while you're using it because then  you're completely vulnerable to  everything they do but that's going to  be the end of the video today guys if  you have any other questions definitely  leave it in the comments below I'll try  to answer all of them if need be and if  you have any other tips that I didn't  put in the video that you think is worth  noting about the specific weapon also  putting that in the comments below for  other people to know so we can all get  caught up on the info subscribe if  you're new I'm covering a lot more of  these guides on for tonight especially  with the new weapons coming up that seem  to be every single week we're getting  new stuff and if there's a new type of  landing spot like a point of interest  I'm going to be covering that and  specific you know for example lucky  landing if anything else new similar to  that comes out I'll be covering guides  on those as well as other tips to make  everybody a better player whether that  be building or anything on the offense  defense all the type of stuff I'm gonna  I have guides coming out for some of  that stuff in the future my two most  recent videos are gonna be on screen if  you guys do want to check that out and  with that guys hope you have a great  rest of your day and peace out

